{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXD5hfxbRHiBDq14LUo7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Full playback of the reading**\n\n**Question the board answers:** How does a Fernhouse customer start a return in the app?\n\n**Outcome:** The product and support team can see each step from the order list to the confirmation, and where the 30-day window sends a customer to Contact support.\n\n**Dials:** Balanced detail, Mixed audience, Laptop distance.\n\n**Sources:** The app and the returns doc, as you described them. No screenshots. Both are current behavior, and the free pickup is a proposal.\n\n**Outline, in drawing order**\n1. Order list\n2. Order detail, from the order list\n3. Decision \"Within 30 days of delivery?\", from the order detail\n4. Start a return button, from the decision on Yes\n5. Contact support, from the decision on No\n6. Return reasons, from the Start a return button\n7. Decision \"Drop-off point or courier pickup?\", from the return reasons\n8. Confirmation with a QR code, from the decision on each of its two exits\n\nThat is 8 nodes and 8 connectors, with 3 labelled exits.\n\n**Two framings**\n- **Happy path with the branch beside it, recommended.** The main row runs from the order list to the confirmation, and Contact support branches off at the 30-day decision. It costs a second look to see the two states of the order detail, but it reads as one customer journey.\n- **State map.** It draws the order detail twice, with the button and with Contact support. It shows both states directly, but it adds a node and splits the row.\n\n**Look I'd propose**\n- The first glance is the 30-day decision, because that is where a customer gets sent to support.\n- The goal is the confirmation with the QR code, named without the accent.\n- No zones, since 8 nodes fit one row.\n- The title is \"Start a return\".\n- The subtitle is \"How a Fernhouse customer starts a return in the app, from the order list to a confirmation with a QR code\".\n- The source line is \"Sources: the app and the returns doc. Left out: free pickup over 100 euros, a proposal under review.\"\n\n**What I've assumed, and what would settle it**\n- **Reader:** the product and support team. A source naming the reader would settle it.\n- **Must not:** no free pickup step and nothing after the confirmation. You can say otherwise.\n- **Window check:** it sits on the order detail, which you confirmed.\n- **Target:** a new section in file `<test-file-key>`, in the Fernhouse Product plan as you stated it. I haven't confirmed that plan myself.\n\n**Left out:** free pickup over 100 euros (a proposal under review), and everything after the confirmation.\n\nIs this reading right, or what should change?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":917,"cache_read_input_tokens":66619,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":917},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"691ecf52-8e50-4c94-9ad5-a02eea5ddef8","uuid":"6b4a3ebc-743c-404e-b521-7539f1fe2e34","timestamp":"2026-10-29T21:06:25.021Z","request_id":"req_011CgXD5hQLBh1aZfWq3s6bH"}
